//==
// # The Green oracle computed once per face (complexity sweep, chunk L5)
//
// Layer 07's area and volume oracles run each face's Green boundary at two resolutions and
// extrapolate (Richardson); the value and its allowance both read the same two results. Before this
// chunk each reader rebuilt them: Oracle_FaceAreaByGreen and GreenAllowance together built the
// boundary 5 to 7 times per face. A GreenEstimate holds the two results once, so the value and the
// allowance are derived from one pair (GreenAreaPair, ShellVolumePair).

// The two Green results of a face or a shell, at n and 2n chords per coedge, and what the
// allowance and the area tolerance read from the boundaries that made them.
// Ran is false when the oracle cannot run (CanGreen false, a shell out of range): every number is
// then NaN and FineSegments 0. FineSegments is the number of segments of the 2n-chord boundary
// (summed over the faces for a shell): the rounding term of the allowance. ConeRadius is the
// smallest |R + v tan a| over the n-chord boundary of a face on a cone (FaceSmallestConeRadius),
// NaN on other surfaces and for a shell.
// Removes: the boundary rebuilt by every reader of the oracle's value and allowance.
type GreenEstimate
{
    Ran: Boolean;
    Coarse: Number;
    Fine: Number;
    FineSegments: Integer;
    ConeRadius: Number;
}
